WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.455
Have a file on your PC and want to open it on your phone?

2
00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:04.910
Click Share to a device.

3
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.093
Choose the folder you want to share.

4
00:00:07.093 --> 00:00:10.427
Pick the local network and how long access should last.

5
00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:14.185
You can also add a password, so the link isn't open to anyone.

6
00:00:14.185 --> 00:00:17.944
When sharing starts, Arus shows a Q R code and a private link.

7
00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.126
Connect your phone to the same WiFi.

8
00:00:20.126 --> 00:00:24.249
Scan the Q R code, then browse the folder from your phone's browser.

9
00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:27.825
You can open files or download them straight to the device.

10
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:30.432
The server runs only on your local network.

11
00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:35.767
There's no internet access, and sharing stops when you press Stop sharing or close Arus.

12
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:39.222
You can start sharing again later with the same settings.

13
00:00:39.222 --> 00:00:43.284
The shared folder stays on your PC; it isn't uploaded to the cloud.

14
00:00:43.284 --> 00:00:47.952
It's a quick way to move files without a cable or an extra app on your phone.

15
00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:51.043
Just remember to keep the private link to yourself.

